  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "t0T5ja292EPpKE6Bayfz66isdQw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:50.487Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The integration is a CiviCRM post-hook dispatching typed operations on membership state change. Membership transitions are the right unit because they are the events an association is actually asked about: when someone joined, when their status changed, and who changed it.\n\nTwo acceptance criteria are recorded, and both are external to CiviCRM's own guarantees. The record must survive a CiviCRM upgrade, and it must satisfy an association's audit. The second is a stronger test than a technical one \u2014 the record has to be legible to an auditor, not merely present in a table.\n\nThe single lead is SYSTOPIA GmbH in Bonn, marked \"1 \u00b7 start here\". Its tool column reads \"CiviCRM-class membership tooling\" rather than CiviCRM outright, so the specific product is characterised by category rather than confirmed; the hook name in the demo text presumes CiviCRM itself, and that presumption is worth checking before the demo is scoped.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**1 \u00b7 start here**\n- SYSTOPIA GmbH (DE Bonn) \u2014 Fabian Schuttenberg + Martin Peth, Gesch\u00e4ftsf\u00fchrer \u00b7 info@systopia.de \u00b7 https://systopia.de\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> CiviCRM post-hook dispatching typed operations on membership state change \u2014 a lifecycle record that survives a CiviCRM upgrade and satisfies an association's audit.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:31:50.487432Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:31:50.487436Z"
    }
  },
